     "text": "{\"count\": 0, \"rationale\": \"No single blocked step makes crownData:exfiltrate unreachable, because every step has an alternative route around it. The target is an OR of four collection steps. codeRepo:collection needs appServer:lateralMovement. appServer:lateralMovement is an OR that tokenCache:credentialAccess alone satisfies, and tokenCache comes straight from the footholds. shareMount:collection is an OR of appServer:lateralMovement, monitoringHost:lateralMovement and secretsManager:privilegeEscalation. monitoringHost is reachable through memoryDump:credentialAccess, which comes from iotDevice:exploitPublicApp or containerHost:exploitPublicApp, both reachable from footholds. Blocking appServer leaves shareMount open via monitoringHost. Blocking monitoringHost or memoryDump leaves codeRepo open via appServer. Blocking tokenCache leaves appServer open via sshKey or memoryDump. Other paths (vaultRead, dbReplica) add further redundancy.\"}"
    }
